- **{{ theme.name }} {{ v.variant.name }}** — {{ v.variant.description }}
{% endfor %}
## Install

### User theme (quickest, for local use)

Copy the generated theme into Zed's themes directory:

```sh
mkdir -p ~/.config/zed/themes
cp {{ theme.id }}.json ~/.config/zed/themes/{{ theme.id }}.json
```

Zed picks it up immediately. Open the theme selector with
`cmd-k cmd-t` (macOS) / `ctrl-k ctrl-t` (Linux), or set it in `settings.json`:

{% if darks | length > 0 and lights | length > 0 -%}
```json
{
  "theme": {
    "mode": "system",
    "light": "{{ theme.name }} {{ lights.0.variant.name }}",
    "dark": "{{ theme.name }} {{ darks.0.variant.name }}"
  }
}
```
{% else -%}
```json
{ "theme": "{{ theme.name }} {{ first.variant.name }}" }
```
{% endif %}
### As an extension

Zed themes can also be distributed as an extension via the
[extensions repository](https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions). Place
`{{ theme.id }}.json` under a `themes/` directory in an extension named `{{ theme.id }}` with an
`extension.toml`, then publish or install as a dev extension
(`zed: install dev extension`).

## Regenerate

```sh
cargo run --features generator -- generate-theme --theme-dir themes/{{ theme.id }} --tool zed --out-dir dist
```
